                        lib/Makefile.am.

                        Gotchas for any future Config sub-block writer (none yet
                        planned; Phase 11/13 are postponed):

                        (i) BYTES round-trip via GBytes. ipv4_config,
                        public_key, private_key are length-delimited
                        bytes sub-fields.  Stash them on PnMeshState as
                        GBytes* (own-on-parse, free-on-close, clear in
                        clear_state) and ref+copy into a per-call struct in the
                        async wrapper so the worker thread sees a stable input
                        even if the page rebuilds its ctx mid-flight.

                        (ii) REPEATED bytes (admin_key). Same recipe but a
                        GPtrArray-of-GBytes with g_bytes_unref as the free func,
                        allocated up front in open_sync and set_size(0) at the
                        top of each parse pass. The async wrapper deep-copies
                        the array (g_bytes_ref each entry) before handing it to
                        the thread.

                        (iii) "I understand" check. Reset to FALSE on every
                        set_state and after a successful Apply -- a sticky check
                        would let a user accidentally re-Apply a stale config
                        after a handshake gave fresh data.

