               field. Default "" follows the primary SSH Login profile
               (user-chosen "mirror" behaviour); with NONE configured it
               resolves to ambient -> today's behaviour preserved.
               THREAD-SAFETY: every SSH node runs its blocking ssh on a
               PnAutoTrigger worker thread, but pn_node_get_profile reads the
               GObject property + the mutable vault and is main-thread-only.
               So pn_ssh_build_argv was revised (47.3 took a live PnProfile*)
               to take a flat value snapshot PnSshLogin (username / identity /
               host-key-policy / port; secrets NOT included). New core helpers
               in lib/pn-ssh-profile.{c,h}: pn_ssh_login_resolve (main-thread
               profile -> snapshot), _copy, _clear, _refresh (resolve +
               swap-under-mutex), _dup_locked (worker reads the cached
               snapshot), pn_ssh_auth_profile_param_spec. Each node caches a
               PnSshLogin under its existing mutex, refreshed from the
               property setter AND a PnVault::changed handler (live credential
               edits), and the worker dups it before building the argv. tmux-
               monitor threads the snapshot through tm_build_argv into both its
               periodic-capture and session-enumerator ssh paths.
               Tests: test-pn-ssh-build-argv reworked onto PnSshLogin (215
               checks) + a pn_ssh_login_resolve case (tiny PnNode subclass +
               vault profile; ambient / follow-primary / explicit-id / custom-
               sentinel, secret-leak guard); test-pn-shell-command wrap_argv
               calls updated for the new login param. 131 C unit tests + plugin
               -load / gui-companion / credentials-profile / shell-companion
               python regressions all green. No inline "Custom settings" entry
               (SSH nodes carry no inline auth, so the picker shows Default +
               profiles only). Password/passphrase feeding still 47.5.
               REWORKED by the 2026-06-08 REDESIGN: the picker now DOES offer a
               "Custom settings" entry whose single inline field is the node's
               existing "host" property, so host comes from the node only in
               Custom mode and from the credential otherwise; PnSshLogin gains a
               host field. See 47.10.
         [x] 47.5 Password auth: BatchMode=yes forbids any prompt, so a
               password-auth profile needs a non-interactive path (sshpass-style
               feeding or libssh). Decide whether to support password auth at all
               or restrict the type to key/agent auth in v1; if we keep
               BatchMode, document that password fields are key-passphrase only.
               (Respect the "pure C, no helper subprocess" rule -- prefer libssh
               over shelling out to sshpass if we go password-capable.)
               DECIDED (2026-06-08, Q-confirmed): RESTRICT v1 to ssh-agent /
               unencrypted-key auth; keep BatchMode=yes on the spawned ssh; do
               NOT add a non-interactive feeding path. KEY REALISATION: BatchMode
               suppresses EVERY prompt, so it blocks the encrypted-key passphrase
               prompt as much as the password one -- under the current subprocess
               model NEITHER stored secret can be replayed. So v1 auth is
               agent / unencrypted-key only; an encrypted key must be unlocked via
               ssh-add, password auth is unsupported. The "password" and
               "passphrase" SECRET fields stay in the schema (scrubbed, vault-only)
               so the future non-interactive path -- the libssh PnSshSession weighed
               in 47.7 -- can adopt them without a schema change; they are simply
               never sent today. No new dependency, no parallel connection path
               (libssh deferred to 47.7/#28). DONE as a documented decision +
               wording: SshProfile.html gains a "Which authentication works (v1)"
               section + ssh-add step and corrected passphrase/password rows;
               pn-ssh-profile.c password/passphrase tooltips + the secrets comment
               record the decision; pn_ssh_build_argv's header doc updated. Tests
               unchanged & green (test-pn-ssh-profile 35, test-pn-ssh-build-argv
               215). NOTE for the REDESIGN: 47.9's "password" auth-schema choice
               stays REACHABLE in the combobox per the redesign, but its help/
               tooltips must carry this "not sent in v1" caveat; revisit if 47.7
               lands the libssh path.
