         [-] 47.7 Session helper(s) to initiate AND maintain an SSH connection.
               WONTFIX (2026-06-08, decided in chat): the per-fire-handshake cost
               is real but is the SAME cross-cutting "single-owner / stateful
               resource reused across fires" problem that MANY plugins share (the
               #28 list: serial/MQTT/Zigbee/Meshtastic/kodi/...). Solving it once
               here, node-by-node, with an SSH-only ControlMaster or libssh path
               would invent a parallel lifetime model just for SSH. Nothing is
               broken today -- it is a performance optimization, not a correctness
               fix -- so we will NOT do an SSH-local version. The eventual fix is
               the elaborate host-managed shared-session layer (#28, ABI v6); SSH
               plugs into that as #28's item (e) when it lands. The decision-only
               output of 47.7 ("(a) vs (b), defer-until-#28?") = DEFER, via #28,
               not via a standalone SSH session helper. No code, no schema change.
               (Closes the implementation side of 47.7; 47.8-47.11 redesign items
               are independent and still open.)
               --- original analysis kept for #28's eventual SSH port ---
               TODAY THERE IS NONE: every SSH node g_spawn's a fresh one-shot
               `ssh <host> <cmd>` on each fire (host-monitoring via
               g_spawn_command_line_sync, shell via g_spawn_sync), so each tick
               pays a full TCP + auth handshake and nothing is kept alive between
               fires. Add a small helper API the nodes call instead of spawning
               raw -- e.g. pn_ssh_session_open(host, profile) -> handle +
               pn_ssh_session_run(handle, argv) -> output + pn_ssh_session_close
               -- that owns ONE authenticated connection per (host, profile) and
               reuses it across fires. Two viable implementations to weigh:
                 (a) OpenSSH ControlMaster multiplexing: keep building an ssh
                     argv but add `-o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=...`
                     and a per-(host,profile) ControlPath socket, so the 2nd..Nth
                     `ssh` reuse one authenticated channel. Smallest change,
                     stays on the existing spawn path, no new dep.
                 (b) A long-lived libssh-backed PnSshSession object held by the
                     host (no per-fire subprocess at all -- aligns with the
                     "pure C, no helper subprocess" rule and with the async/exec
                     model). Heavier, adds the libssh dep, but is the clean home
                     for keepalive + connection-state reporting.
               This is the SSH instance of the single-owner/stateful-resource
               problem TODO #28 (host-managed shared profile sessions, ABI v6)
               describes for serial/MQTT; if #28's shared-session machinery
               lands first, the SSH session pool should plug into it rather than
               invent a parallel lifetime model. Decide (a) vs (b) -- and whether
               to defer 47.7 until #28 -- before implementing.

